  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Each stem has exactly one plural noun to replace. Never two plurals.",
      "The correct pronoun is they, them, we, or us. Never a singular pronoun.",
      "Use they when that plural noun does the action. Use them when it receives the action.",
      "Use we or us only when the stem group clearly includes I or me. Otherwise they or them.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are far singular pronouns such as he, she, or it.",
      "Tier 2 distractors mix wrong case they or them with we or us when the speaker is not in the group.",
      "Tier 3 distractors are near-miss plural pronouns they, them, we, and us.",
      "Never write a stem that can take two right pronouns.",
      "Keep stems in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands.",
      "Use <NAME> for any person name. Never a real name."
    ]
  },
