  "tier_rules": {
    "1": "Short stems of three to five words and one regular plural. Picture the noun. they or them is obvious. Distractors are far singular he, she, or it.",
    "2": "Stems of four to seven words with two-syllable kid words. Mix subject they and object them. Distractors include wrong case and we or us when I is not in the group.",
    "3": "Near misses: a time phrase before the subject, an irregular plural, or a group with I or me that needs we or us. Distractors are the other plural pronouns."
  },
  "miss_explain": {
